{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:04:56.245930Z","id":"c0375dfc8269930c54452a085ce634c4f3af85fe5ef5d6ab78ecb55d61abb9ae","body":{"detail":"Synthesized NSEvent pointer moves do not reach WebKit while the test app is not the active app (macOS refuses activation to a process launched behind another), so the shell never sees the mouseover that counts the pointer's arrival (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts condition 3). The test therefore sends claxHost.attestPointer down, as the app screen's listener does for a finger, before the click. A run with the app active and real mouse input (L1 or a manual check) is still needed for the macOS pointer path. The test also does not cover the inter-app read with consent (spec section 3.8), which needs a click on the shell's consent prompt.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":398},"end":{"line":413},"content_hash":"110d3bb93d15b8bba3e4ef226e7f56f8d9efa35649db0676116382ce1b3fa770"},"summary":"The macOS integration test attests the press itself: it does not verify that a real pointer's arrival on the frame counts in a WKWebView","tags":["test-gap","macos","f10","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:31:46.114067Z","id":"0a999fa91f6083052133f7143b544655cbcbebd480d04b861f31d9d3dba26e17","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c0375dfc8269930c54452a085ce634c4f3af85fe5ef5d6ab78ecb55d61abb9ae","summary":"The inter-app read with consent is covered since 60edd01b (scripted second app, real click on the shell's Allow, read and grant asserted). The pointer-arrival gap stands.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:56:25.500952Z","id":"44c5dca67986978346d6c3880b4a75973b667b82cb9bc1b6aedf82086f7237de","body":{"detail":"flutter test integration_test -d macos (via scripts/build-app-clax.sh macos first) printed 'All tests passed!' and exited 0 after 92 s, yet build/macos/Build/Products/Debug/clax_app.app/Contents/MacOS/clax_app (PPID 1, started with the run) was still running 80 s later, with no clax child left (the rig's supervisor had stopped the daemon). It was stopped by its PID. A gate or script that runs this test should find the app's PID (for example from a file the rig writes) and stop it, since AGENTS.md forbids finding it by name pattern.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"5757c760678bc13830abfe8cbb4f9b0b90d5dcaca3701c3069dfab08bc528e92"},"summary":"After a passing run the debug clax_app process can outlive flutter test, reparented to launchd","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T15:18:57.151672Z","id":"86d15c167359b11bc58513b5e37b8b2340df683c527659ce79632063daed2abb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:ca792e6b","summary":"Fixed in ca792e6b (macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift, debug only). Cause found by logging ppid at launch: after a fresh build, a second clax_app instance starts under launchd (ppid 1, the tool's environment) about 1 s after the tool's own child; no test drives it and the tool never stops it. Such an instance now exits at once, and the tool's child quits when the tool's process ends. Evidence: two rebuild runs of flutter test integration_test/full_loop_test.dart -d macos, both 'All tests passed!', and 15 s later ps lists no Debug/clax_app.app process (before the fix the same check found one after each rebuild run: PIDs 89201, 97360, 3200, 18153, 47360).","supersedes":"44c5dca67986978346d6c3880b4a75973b667b82cb9bc1b6aedf82086f7237de","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/tool_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:12:55.276894Z","id":"8dd9011eb35e6e07ee1c8a0af89d529f28b99e08737daa940c7fd22c44415ab2","body":{"detail":"Run 2026-10-13 (flutter test integration_test/tool_loop_test.dart -d macos): the make passed every assertion (render ToolOk with a PNG, no console errors or failed requests, tests {passed: 1, failed: [], skipped: 0}, finish ToolOk, title Counter, harness app, counter/c {n: 3}, probe label Count); it then timed out waiting for 'app-panel' with keys {inspector-cover, app-cover}. The change (str_replace, render, finish), the landing in place, the kept document and the empty listDrafts have not run yet. full_loop_test.dart passes alone (one of two runs timed out at 'the reader page reporting its read', the rerun passed). Running both files in one 'flutter test integration_test -d macos' twice failed to launch the second file ('The log reader stopped unexpectedly'), both times after the first file failed or while another agent's macOS build held build.db.","kind":"concern","summary":"The tool-loop integration test fails at the panel until blocker 66663ece (hand-over cover) is fixed; past that point it is unproven","tags":["integration","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/tool_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:33:35.587425Z","id":"7b50f4be87cf39558f00b365fbfb7413b063cb70b65e0e25c49c34fa08562b91","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:97712168","summary":"Fixed: with 6fb389da the tool-loop test runs to the end. 'flutter test integration_test/full_loop_test.dart -d macos' (which now runs tool_loop.dart's test, then the full loop): '01:23 +2: All tests passed!' (target/flutter-app/i1-merged.log). The make, the change landing in place with counter/c kept, the resolved thread and the empty listDrafts all pass.","supersedes":"8dd9011eb35e6e07ee1c8a0af89d529f28b99e08737daa940c7fd22c44415ab2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/rig.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T05:14:26.400742Z","id":"309c238725aadc7f7cf15e7bbcf8e5687842eb608d031528eb3f5f8314ab5632","body":{"detail":"Observed 2026-10-14 with load averages 50-380 (other builds plus a CPU burner), logs under target/flutter-app/fl/: full_loop_test.dart timed out at the 45 s cap waiting for 'version 2 landing' (shell messages end at Sent: no ThreadsMsg after the send; fix1.log, fix2.log, exp4.log, load2.log), 'the composer' (exp3.log) and 'the launcher' (still on the splash; load2.log). Twice a run stopped making progress inside a pump: the tool-loop test hit its 5 min Timeout with \"'!_expectingFrame': is not true\" (run5.log), and locked_daemon_test.dart sat idle at 0% CPU for 13 minutes before it was stopped (locked.log). The same files passed 3/3 (full loop) and 1/1 (locked daemon) at load average 6-25 afterwards (fix4-6.log, locked2.log). Not diagnosed: whether 'version 2 landing' is only slow under load or a worker stall, and why a pump stops returning (an occluded macOS window reports AppLifecycleState.hidden and Flutter stops scheduling frames; the rig's lifecycle log was empty in the reported timeouts).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":46},"end":{"line":47},"content_hash":"991c854080a82c716ac4c0ab3002f27aaf8cbbd7ac08aa80f8fe1178fd6a53a6"},"summary":"Under heavy machine load the macOS integration tests time out at steps other than the consent dialog, and some runs hang in a pump","tags":["integration","flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328735Z","id":"f444e97d9fc2060635864b17c9c54b430f6819daee9acef14748d522545906d3","body":{"detail":"Failure: 'make, change, undo and recover on the embedded daemon' at full_loop_test.dart:94 (rig.reloadNewer(tester, 2)): 'timed out waiting for the New version toast; the screen shows (Threads, Versions, Call it My runs, “Runs” · v1 · 2 comments · resolved) ... covering: {AppScreen: 1, ModalBarrier: 1, WebView: 1}; the shell said: [... Sent, ThreadsMsg, NewerMsg]'. Seen 2026-10-17 with bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_full_loop (FAILED in 171.9s) and with cd apps/clax_app && flutter test integration_test/full_loop_test.dart -d macos (02:36 +1 -1), both with the same Bazel-built clax_opt as the embedded daemon (the native run's in build-native/macos/clax), on the branch rebased onto main 146251c4. The first test of the file passes in both. The shell posts NewerMsg, so the daemon and the shell report the new version; a ModalBarrier is up over the app screen, which may hide or delay the toast. Whether it passed before the rebase onto main was not checked.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"0d6658dcf0547496bfed0221b63e754877a94bdfdf5ea2f8d9405d52dc363656"},"summary":"full_loop_test's second test times out waiting for the New version toast, under flutter test and under Bazel alike","tags":["integration","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:00:45.378479Z","id":"0a63cb11ae10ba552c452eb0badf59c39e0133d93fb92fcf30f87e405d194baf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f444e97d9fc2060635864b17c9c54b430f6819daee9acef14748d522545906d3","summary":"Failure: integration_test/full_loop_test.dart 'make, change, undo and recover on the embedded daemon' (flutter test integration_test/full_loop_test.dart -d macos) times out waiting for the New version toast when the embedded daemon is built from this branch after its rebase onto main 146251c4; it passes with the daemon built from flutter-app-pre-main-rebase-2026-10-17. Runs on 2026-10-17, all with the pre-rebase app and test code (a clean copy at target/pre-rebase; the app's Dart and the integration tests did not change in the rebase) and only the embedded clax swapped: pre-rebase daemon (cargo release) passed 2 of 2; the rebased daemon failed 6 of 8 (cargo release of HEAD 26d37aba6 and Bazel's clax_opt alike). The web UI the two daemons embed is byte-identical (shasum of every web/dist file), and so are the shell's and the stream worker's response headers. What happens, from debugPrints added to the copy's lib/ui/app_screen.dart: the worker lands version 2 (WorkerLanded at T), the app offers the toast at once, the toast times out after newerFor (8 s), and the shell's `newer` for version 2 arrives at T+35 s, by which time the offer is spent ('known'), so no toast shows and the rig waits forever. In passing runs `newer` arrives within 0.2 s of the landing. 35 s is web/shell/src/stream.ts DEAD_MS: the page counts its hub dead after 35 s without a ping and reconnects, so in the failing runs the hub the app's shell follows (a SharedWorker, or a leader tab over Web Locks) stops talking to it after the comment is sent. Why the rebased daemon makes that happen was not found; the route table, routes/stream.rs, clax-realtime's stream hub and the compression rules match the pre-rebase ones. Two things to look at next: the daemon's handling of the stream worker's connection (main's crate split moved the listener tuning, the live-page filter and the web UI's FileTree), and the app screen offering a spent toast again when the shell's `newer` comes late (lib/ui/app_screen.dart NewerMsg: `known` suppresses it).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:01:04.687945Z","id":"4e7a8d29c5cf799daa444d834b4ccca91daaafd2baaed432ce5f74a594a83d01","body":{"detail":"Failure: integration_test/full_loop_test.dart 'make, change, undo and recover on the embedded daemon' (flutter test integration_test/full_loop_test.dart -d macos) times out waiting for the New version toast when the embedded daemon is built from this branch after its rebase onto main 146251c4; it passes with the daemon built from flutter-app-pre-main-rebase-2026-10-17. Runs on 2026-10-17, all with the pre-rebase app and test code (a clean copy at target/pre-rebase; the app's Dart and the integration tests did not change in the rebase) and only the embedded clax swapped: pre-rebase daemon (cargo release) passed 2 of 2; the rebased daemon failed 6 of 8 (cargo release of HEAD 26d37aba6 and Bazel's clax_opt alike). The web UI the two daemons embed is byte-identical (shasum of every web/dist file), and so are the shell's and the stream worker's response headers. What happens, from debugPrints added to the copy's lib/ui/app_screen.dart: the worker lands version 2 (WorkerLanded at T), the app offers the toast at once, the toast times out after newerFor (8 s), and the shell's `newer` for version 2 arrives at T+35 s, by which time the offer is spent ('known'), so no toast shows and the rig waits forever. In passing runs `newer` arrives within 0.2 s of the landing. 35 s is web/shell/src/stream.ts DEAD_MS: the page counts its hub dead after 35 s without a ping and reconnects, so in the failing runs the hub the app's shell follows (a SharedWorker, or a leader tab over Web Locks) stops talking to it after the comment is sent. Why the rebased daemon makes that happen was not found; the route table, routes/stream.rs, clax-realtime's stream hub and the compression rules match the pre-rebase ones. Two things to look at next: the daemon's handling of the stream worker's connection (main's crate split moved the listener tuning, the live-page filter and the web UI's FileTree), and the app screen offering a spent toast again when the shell's `newer` comes late (lib/ui/app_screen.dart NewerMsg: `known` suppresses it).","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":90},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"0d6658dcf0547496bfed0221b63e754877a94bdfdf5ea2f8d9405d52dc363656"},"summary":"Since the rebase onto main, the shell's word of a landed change can come 35 s late, and full_loop's second test fails","supersedes":"f444e97d9fc2060635864b17c9c54b430f6819daee9acef14748d522545906d3","tags":["integration","regression","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:01:59.489110Z","id":"4b4a82e89f2f8c81c52a6e8c993503a83722115b177096eba1292eaa57e4757e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:635cffe69","summary":"Fixed in 635cffe69; the cause was in the shell's stream worker, not the rebased daemon. The pre-rebase daemon fails the same way (2 of 3 runs, flutter test with only the embedded clax swapped). Daemon request and stream logs plus page beacons (2026-10-17) showed WebKit (pid of com.apple.WebKit, TIME_WAIT on its side) closing the shared worker's /api/stream connection during the comment click, about 35 s after load, and a new instance of web/shell/src/stream-worker.ts receiving a connect for the tab's still-open port; that instance had no hello or topics, opened no stream and sent no pings, so the tab heard nothing until DEAD_MS (35 s). 635cffe69 has the worker post `welcome` on each connect and the page's worker link send its hello, topics and focus again. web/shell/src/stream-worker.test.ts fails before it (expected 2 /api/stream requests, got 1) and passes after. With the fix: bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_full_loop --runs_per_test=8 --cache_test_results=no PASSED 8 of 8 (min 82.1 s, max 219.9 s); with page beacons, runs where WebKit relaunched the worker recovered at once (welcome, topics resent, new stream) and passed.","supersedes":"4e7a8d29c5cf799daa444d834b4ccca91daaafd2baaed432ce5f74a594a83d01","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:01:59.715352Z","id":"5cca4ecdcfbbcc4456734d0acf52f3ed97907955cf1946607c2df0ba36de5b11","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_full_loop --runs_per_test=8 on 2026-10-17 at 635cffe69's tree: runs 1 and 6 failed with 'timed out waiting for the composer' (rig.comment, line 92; the shell said no DraftClipMsg after the click), run 8 with 'timed out waiting for version 4 offered or shown' (line 169, after the restarted daemon's new shell document); the next batch of 8 passed 8 of 8, and flutter test runs of the file passed 7 of 8 (the one failure: the tool-loop test's 'Couldn't make that change: the script ended without finishing'). None of these was diagnosed, and whether they predate 635cffe69 is not known: before it the test failed earlier, at the version 2 toast.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":92},"end":{"line":94},"content_hash":"fa720b09e527c75d57721143013b2dd6a0de8473913e322bd9a437562e9f17ce"},"summary":"full_loop_test's second test also times out at other steps, at times: the composer after the click, and version 4 offered after the daemon restart","tags":["integration","flaky","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:10:46.720091Z","id":"6b66aedb01b18cfdf6dbcf7f258e9265a14544d0ec792586d9f1ea53891b33a3","body":{"detail":"Version 4: page beacons and daemon request logs (2026-10-17, Bazel batch run 4 of 8) showed the restarted daemon's new shell document post Ready v4 (latest 4, after init) because the held change published version 4 before the app reloaded the shell; Rig.reloadNewer's probe answered false for that case and Rig.until counts false as not yet (apps/clax_app/integration_test/rig.dart), so it waited out its cap. c67e74c7a returns NewerSeen.shown instead; with it, two clean batches of bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_full_loop --runs_per_test=8 had no version 4 timeout (each failed 1 of 8, both in the tool-loop test: see the concern on apps/clax_app/integration_test/tool_loop.dart:76:80). Composer: seen in 2 of 8 runs of one batch on 635cffe69's tree, then in none of 32 runs (16 instrumented with page beacons, 16 clean); in the failing runs the shell said no StateMsg after the click, so the pick was not taken or never reached the shell.","kind":"comment","references":"5cca4ecdcfbbcc4456734d0acf52f3ed97907955cf1946607c2df0ba36de5b11","summary":"The version 4 timeout was the rig's, fixed in c67e74c7a; the composer timeout did not recur in 32 Bazel runs and stays undiagnosed","tags":["integration","flaky","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/tool_loop.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T23:10:46.720395Z","id":"0fa1c4d7785a402e5b89cb9344f1088fae877e8ef4c99923d1d2ccd63a5f01aa","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_full_loop --runs_per_test=8 at c67e74c7a's tree, two batches on 2026-10-17: one run failed at tool_loop.dart:140 (_expectCleanRender: tests {'not_run': 'The tests did not run: it did not load within 10 seconds.'}, the inspector's readyLimit in apps/clax_app/lib/ui/inspector_surface.dart:285), and one at tool_loop.dart:80 ('timed out waiting for version 2 offered or shown' with the working pill and the inspector cover still up, so the scripted change had not finished). A flutter test run of the file earlier failed once with 'Couldn't make that change: the script ended without finishing'. Not diagnosed; each looks like the inspect taking longer than its fixed limits on a loaded machine (record 309c2387 on rig.dart notes load timeouts), but that was not shown.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"804f7138d1fcaf3c78272f0ebe5c464dcc62319a72580bd94ed33afc7618d0b4"},"summary":"The tool-loop test (run first in full_loop_test.dart) fails about 1 run in 8 under Bazel: the render's tests not loading within 10 s, or version 2 not offered","tags":["integration","flaky","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T21:50:19.977193Z","id":"989efe5f25e66921947d0460d2b6e41db921ad276ba3468205740360c54d4ebf","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"c0375dfc8269930c54452a085ce634c4f3af85fe5ef5d6ab78ecb55d61abb9ae","summary":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/mac_chrome_test.dart clicks the page's heading with a pointer move first and nothing attested, and expects a pick when the app is active. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_mac_chrome --test_env=CLAX_MAC_SHOTS_DIR=$PWD/target/flutter-app/mac at f0fece8d4 PASSED, on a locked display (the app inactive: windows drawn from their layers, events handed to their views, key checks skipped; see docs/usage.md): the inactive app's click picked nothing, as this record describes; the owner's run on an unlocked Mac decides it.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/scheme_spike.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.369833Z","id":"c81c5ae99172d357de3160a414d749d3a30802cc70af5be98bb22f0dad1a1056","body":{"detail":"The frame fires fetch and <img> for the shell's URL eight times with setTimeout(0) when told to race (lines 354-367), almost all before the reload's policy decision opens the permit; and the check at lines 515-540 counts a reload with no shell as a pass on Apple. Baseline: 0 of 25 Mac runs lost the reload on 2026-10-20 (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_scheme_spike --runs_per_test=5, then --runs_per_test=20 --nocache_test_results); in every run the frame's 16 requests were all answered 403 with no number and the navigation's own request came last (CLAX_SPIKE_NOTE race), i.e. the burst ended before the policy opened the permit and the window was never exercised. The run of record f3218c17 that lost it was 1 of 2. A check that proves a fix must exercise the window every run and fail on the loss.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":354},"end":{"line":367},"content_hash":"5c158e42a4efb4e1f62e3ef31fc4520b3b3b2185b1eb940829077f7927a6e65d"},"suggested_fix":"Have the frame keep requesting until its pagehide (setInterval at 0 ms plus a request per fetch completion); assert, on every platform, that the reload committed with a shell whose nonce is one minted under the committed number, and that at least one frame request was answered under that number on Apple (the race was exercised); drop the no-shell branch. Run with --runs_per_test=50 --nocache_test_results; any run without a shell fails.","summary":"The spike's race passes whether or not the residual happens, and its eight-round burst rarely lands in the window, so it measures neither the residual nor a fix","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/scheme_spike.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:26.054704Z","id":"18349349e56395deecde6ccc3776cee6172704982894bcf5e9fd71f403aecf5c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2a26c51f3","summary":"Fixed in 2a26c51f3: the frame asks for the shell's URL by <img>, no-cors fetch and cors fetch on four chains, each always with one request in flight, from before the reload (the shell reloads once the first round is answered) until pagehide; reloadKeptUnderRace requires a shell under a nonce minted for the committed number on every platform, no numbered request with an Origin header, every unnumbered shell-document request 403, and on Apple at least two requests under the committed number; the no-shell branch is gone. It fails on the residual and passes on the fix: Mac, --runs_per_test=50 --nocache_test_results, 50 of 50 failed with e24bae229's one-shot permit and 50 of 50 passed with 89bdc7263.","supersedes":"c81c5ae99172d357de3160a414d749d3a30802cc70af5be98bb22f0dad1a1056","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/integration_test/rig.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:11:43.880521Z","id":"64a50cbacbf20f9223a0e30fdab58bf01cbe127d7d4bd62379a8e1e2b533bb76","body":{"detail":"rig.dart, ios_rig.dart, full_loop_test.dart (its daemon kill and restart step dropped, the held change kept), bundle_test.dart, mac_chrome_test.dart, ios_cold_start_test.dart (core.json's PID instead of daemon.json's) and ios_background_test.dart (no port check) compile (//apps/clax_app:dart_analyze) but no integration target ran them; their page origin expectations are AppOrigins.content(aid), which WebKit's location.origin for the clax scheme has not been checked against in these tests.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"5b43312833cc9bee012231a64b4d3687276495b2a2fd87de4bd00a6275c75cac"},"suggested_fix":"Run //apps/clax_app:integration_full_loop, :integration_bundle, :integration_mac_chrome and the iOS simulator targets once the macOS app ships libclax_embed.dylib.","summary":"The macOS and iOS integration rigs were ported to the core without being run","tags":["core","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
